WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.190
Hi, Conan here.

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:03.500
Welcome back to our show.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.430
We've been off the air
for a couple of weeks,

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.310
and we're back now,

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:08.920
taping once again

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:13.150
in the iconic Largo
theater in Los Angeles.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:18.150
I apologize, still haven't cut
my hair, down over my eyes.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.640
Not really quite sure
where I am right now,

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:21.750
but it doesn't matter.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.130
I'm with you, and that's
the important thing.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:25.110
And we have a terrific show.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:28.110
Jason Sudeikis is here to talk about

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:31.140
his terrific new show, Ted Lasso.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.730
So we'll be talking to
him in just a second.

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:36.840
Now, as I've said, we're
here at the Largo theater,

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.373
just a skeleton crew,

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:41.640
hardly anybody joining me here,

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.743
just to keep things COVID safe.

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:47.240
And let's face it, it's
pretty much an empty theater,

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:48.363
which can get lonely.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.280
And I don't know, I'm not used to that.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.117
I'm used to a crowd chanting

00:00:54.117 --> 00:00:58.700
"We love you, you're the
best, TV icon", whatever.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:02.150
This is new to me, working
in complete silence.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:04.400
And then, check this out,

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.750
I was watching Major League
Baseball this past weekend,

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:09.270
and I got an idea.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.610
Now, you may have seen this.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:13.550
Teams have been filling their empty stands

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:16.460
with cardboard cutouts of fans.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.463
Check it out. See that?

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:21.540
When I heard that idea, I
thought that's not gonna work,

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.710
but it actually looks pretty good.

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:25.910
People are okay with it.

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:30.910
So I asked my crew to bring
me whatever cardboard cutouts

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:35.120
they could find in storage at
our Warner Brothers Studio,

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:37.700
just random cardboard cutouts

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:40.260
that were hanging out
in the props department.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:41.260
And guess what?

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:42.410
Here's what they found.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:43.710
Here's what we got.

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:47.400
We got Ruth Bader Ginsburg, all right?

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.870
We have Conrad Bain.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.053
Remember the dad from Different Strokes?

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:54.860
They found a life-size,
six-foot-six cutout

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:58.220
of former FBI Director, James Comey.

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:00.990
And for some reason, they
found four, count 'em,

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:02.823
four Kevin Harts.

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:06.150
That's my audience right now,

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.920
and I feel pretty good about it.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.480
It actually looks like Comey is standing

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:12.540
to object to some comedy I just did,

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:13.530
but that's not the point.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:17.370
The point is, I need to fill
the rest of the audience,

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.320
and here's my idea.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:22.260
I wanna do it with
cutouts of my actual fans.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.010
I'm not kidding around, this is real.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:28.720
This is your chance to join my audience

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:31.240
in cardboard cutout form.

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:32.580
Okay, we're gonna make this happen.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:33.530
Here's what you do.

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:38.530
Go to teamcoco.com/cutouts and
upload a photo of yourself.

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:42.540
That's right, take a photo of
yourself and then upload it.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:46.880
Be sure to include your
name and city of residence.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:51.880
And then, we may put you right
here in our Largo audience.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:56.690
Now, in the photo, you
can, it's your choice,

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.530
you can be enjoying the show,

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:02.720
or if you choose, you
cannot be enjoying the show.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:04.600
See, if everyone in the
audience, if I look over there,

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.790
and every single person in the audience

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:08.220
is enjoying the show,

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.070
that's not gonna feel realistic to me.

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:12.810
So once again, here's what you do, okay?

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:14.640
You upload a photo of yourself

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:18.490
and you go to teamcoco.com/cutouts,

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.760
and you'll get all the
details there on how to do it.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.610
And who knows, you may get to sit

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:27.830
next to former FBI Director, James Comey,

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:28.730
night after night.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:33.730
You may get to sit in-between
two of the four Kevin Harts.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.790
Anything can happen.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:37.290
The sky's the limit.

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:38.560
So let's make this happen,

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:40.960
and I'll give you a
shout out on television.

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:43.453
See, this quarantine isn't so bad.

